      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The availability of potent combination antiretroviral therapy has changed the long-term prognosis for people living with HIV/AIDS. There is increasing concern, however, about the effect of HIV therapy on lipid disorders and subsequent development of coronary artery disease. Virtually all classes of antiretroviral drugs have been associated with some aspect of atherogenic changes in the lipid profiles. This article reviews the current literature on HIV-associated dyslipidemias and the metabolic syndrome, their potential effect on future coronary heart disease, and reviews strategies for management."},
